  "question": {
    "text": "A driver in a car, approaching a vertical wall notices that the frequency of his car horn has changed from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>440</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math> to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>480</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>, when it gets reflected from the wall. If the speed of sound in air is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>345</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, then the speed of the car is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>54</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>r</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>r</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>r</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>r</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p>Frequency of sound after reflection from the wall is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>'</mo><mo>'</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>480</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p>Frequency of sound emitted by the horn of car&nbsp;is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>440</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p>Speed of sound is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>345</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>The diver in the car (as a source)&nbsp;approaching the vertical wall which is the observer in this case, The frequency&nbsp;of sound received by the stationary wall is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>'</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mi>f</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>As the frequency&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;is received by wall will act as a source now, and driver in the car is an observer, the frequency of sound received by driver is ,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>'</mo><mo>'</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mi>v</mi></mfrac></mfenced><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Equating equation (1) and (2) we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>'</mo><mo>'</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mi>f</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Substitute the given value in the equation (3), we get<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>480</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>345</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>345</mn><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>440</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>345</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>345</mn><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Velocity of car is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>54</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>hr</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>"
  }
